{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"agent_message","text":"The visual review is complete: the ray, swarm formations, gardener states, finale, portrait layout, and credits are readable. The full campaign replay also exercised scout, guard, hunter, and fallen-teammate states. I’m updating the required feedback and checking the final export, including replay and network result handling.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('interview.json');data=json.loads(p.read_text());data['sourceInformation']['tech']='my-3D2dge v0.89.1 with boot-path fix; AI Hub protocol 1 / client 1.4.0; JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio, WebRTC; Bun 1.3.14 build';data['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unrestricted headless testing, scripted normal-command campaign playthroughs, Chromium/WebKit/Firefox, emulated standard pads and touch, native headless drawing, offline audio and live bus analysis, real Hub harness and two-context WebRTC. Physical devices, public Internet connectivity and subjective listening were unavailable.';data['testingFeedback']=['6 distinct defects caught and fixed; test-fixture and floating-point assertion corrections are recorded separately.','1 critical issue: the upstream boot:false path prevented leaving the title. It is fixed.','The ordinary-command whole-campaign replay, combined with shared-world harness checks: it verified real completion and caught contact ordering and lifecycle defects.','An unbound synthetic pointer event for touch cancellation was less useful than actual browser touch events; it did not represent an active touch. Replaced it with valid cancellation and CDP multitouch tests.'];data['engineFeedback'][1]='The boot:false path left _booting set, blocking scene transitions. Native expand sizing also needed explicit arena containment, including paused resize handling.';data['engineFeedback'][4]='Patched one engine line: boot:false clears _booting before returning to start. Otherwise Play remains on the title. All other game systems extend native APIs; the Hub SDK is pristine.';p.write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('tools/build.mjs');s=p.read_text();needle='console.log(';idx=s.index(needle);s=s[:idx]+'''const interview=JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(root,\\\"interview.json\\\"),\\\"utf8\\\"